+---
+features:
+  - |
+    The Boolean user option ``password_policy_exempt`` explicitly exempts the
+    target identity from password regex checks and SQL self-service password
+    history and minimum-age checks. Password and classification may be sent in
+    the same create or update request. The option uses existing resource-option
+    storage and requires no database migration. It is independent of the native
+    first-use, expiry and lockout exception options.
+security:
+  - |
+    Supplying ``password_policy_exempt`` on user creation or update additionally
+    requires ``identity:manage_password_policy_exemption``, whose default is
+    ``role:admin and system_scope:all`` with no deprecated fallback. The check
+    also protects false values and null removal. Classification assignments are
+    audited without credentials. SQL password checks use transaction-local
+    resource options under a user-row lock instead of cached classification. Old-password authentication, password locks,
+    technical limits and token revocation are preserved.
